# <summary line>                                                     (max 72 chars)
#
# <Why this change, what problem it solves, what it rules out. The 'why',
#  not the 'what' -- the diff already says what. Delete these comment lines;
#  git strips them when the message is edited.>
#
# -- AI attribution ----------------------------------------------------------
# If any advanced coding tool took part in authoring the change, add:
#
#     Assisted-by: LLM [TOOL1] [TOOL2]
#
# The value is literally "LLM", whatever tool you used. The trailing tokens are
# for *analysis* tools (coccinelle, sparse, smatch, clang-tidy), not for the
# assistant. Do NOT name the assistant, its vendor or its model: the Linux
# kernel removed those fields in Aug 2026 because they advertised proprietary
# vendors without telling a reviewer anything useful.
#
# Do NOT use Co-authored-by: or Co-developed-by: for an assistant -- those
# claim authorship and certify the Developer Certificate of Origin, which only
# a human can do. Never add Signed-off-by: on the AI's behalf.
#
# A commit written entirely by a human needs no trailer.
#
# To stamp it automatically instead of typing it:
#     git commit --trailer Assisted-by ...
# (configured via trailer.Assisted-by.cmd; see AGENTS.md)